      "text": [
        " : اَلرَّجُلُ يَدَّهِنُ بِأَيِّ دُهْنٍ شَاءَ إِذَا لَمْ يَكُنْ فِيهِ مِسْكٌ وَ لاَ عَنْبَرٌ وَ لاَ زَعْفَرَانٌ وَ لاَ وَرْسٌ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَغْتَسِلَ لِلْإِحْرَامِ قَالَ «وَ لاَ تُجَمِّرْ ثَوْباً لِإِحْرَامِكَ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2539 - Mu'awiyah ibn Ammar narrated from Imam (as) that a person may anoint themselves with any oil they wish before performing ghusl for Ihram, provided that the oil does not contain:\n-\tMusk\n-\tAmbergris\n-\tSaffron\n-\tWars (a type of yellow plant dye).\nImam (as) also added: \"Do not perfume your Ihram garments with incense (tajmir).\""
        ]
      }
    },
